overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- the sample variance ${S}^{2}$ is an unbiased estimator of the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ and\n\n- ${\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2}={s}^{2}$ denotes an unbiased estimate of ${\\sigma }^{2}$ that's computed from the sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}.$\n\nWe're given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{51}{({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}=24.5$ and $n=51.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n-1}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{51-1}\\cdot 24.5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}\\cdot 24.5 \\\\  & =0.49.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, an unbiased estimate of the population variance is ${\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2}=0.49.$ We take the square root to compute an unbiased estimate of the standard deviation. This gives\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\sigma }=\\sqrt{0.49}=0.7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ba1e9e1a-855b-5e0e-8730-feb174aced84"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ba1e9e1a-855b-5e0e-8730-feb174aced84" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba1e9e1a-855b-5e0e-8730-feb174aced84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-90b3402d-6afa-58de-87a4-ace03f1b7710" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74e5d5fc-d551-5446-8f5a-277c7dc3e028" "answer-f3562734-54c8-5167-889c-5d3f14bb8dea" "answer-26f31e5b-1fa1-56d2-8786-d2c285ab5fa8" "answer-90b3402d-6afa-58de-87a4-ace03f1b7710" "answer-15dde39d-88be-58d2-9cfe-766d0c016346"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74e5d5fc-d551-5446-8f5a-277c7dc3e028" :answer/id #uuid "74e5d5fc-d551-5446-8f5a-277c7dc3e028" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3562734-54c8-5167-889c-5d3f14bb8dea" :answer/id #uuid "f3562734-54c8-5167-889c-5d3f14bb8dea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "an